invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_hw.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the host object's one-pass seal hashes the pass before's plaintext where
  SP 800-38D §7.1 hashes its ciphertext. A seal in place cannot show the
  difference, because the loop reads the pass before's bytes after it
  wrote them over its plaintext, so the two are one buffer; a seal
  into a second buffer, which QUIC's packets take, gets a tag no peer
  verifies. bin/ghash_equiv_test seals into a second buffer as well as in
  place, on both paths, and compares the tags.

--- old
            ghash_hash_pass(&s.ghash, &out[at - GCM_HW_PASS_BYTES]);
--- new
            ghash_hash_pass(&s.ghash, &in[at - GCM_HW_PASS_BYTES]);
